course: dictionary
lesson: 5437
title: Words of sorrow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lament is a word for deep sadness. As a verb, to lament means to show you are very sad, often about a death. «Psalms of lament are prayers of sorrow or complaint» tells you the word is about sorrow, and the rest of the sentence shows that a lament can also be a prayer.
explain: As a noun, a lament is a thing: a sad song, poem or piece of music about loss. Ask yourself: is the word doing something, or is it a thing? That tells you which meaning to use.
explain: To lament can also mean to feel sad and sorry that something has gone or is missing. «Many lament the loss of the village shop» means many people feel sad that the shop has closed. The clue is loss: something is missing.
fact: Lament means to show strong sorrow, or a sad song or poem about loss.
fact: Lament can be a verb (to lament) or a noun (a lament).
fact: «Lament the loss of» means to feel sad that something has gone.
fact: «The late lamented» is a formal way to speak of someone who has died or is gone, and is missed.
fact: Psalm 13 is a psalm of lament, a prayer of sorrow that asks «How long, O Lord?».
exercise: «Psalms of lament are prayers of sorrow or complaint.» What does lament mean here? | *A sad prayer, a cry of sorrow | A loud shout of joy | A long list of names | A happy dance at the harvest festival
exercise: Many people lament the loss of the village shop. What does lament mean here? | Buy lots of things from the shop | Build a new shop | Shout at the shopkeeper | *Feel sad and sorry about something that has gone
exercise: A lament is a sad song or poem about loss. What is a lament? | *A sad song, poem or piece of music about loss | A sort of shop | A kind of bird | A happy party song
test: «Hannah laments that her best friend has moved away.» What does laments mean? | Is painting a picture | *Is very sad and sorry about it | Is running a race | Is laughing and dancing
test: In «a lament for the lost king», what kind of word is lament? | *A noun, a sad song or poem | A verb, an action word | A question word | An adjective, a describing word
exam: Which phrase means someone who has died and is still missed? | the early bird | *the late lamented | a lamp post | a lost sock
